G-PK2-PREFILL — the >~1000-token daemon prefill "stall" RESOLVED (2026-07-07)
==============================================================================
Contract: lattice papers/CONTRACT-PRODUCT-KEYSTONE-2.md §T1
Handoff:  START-HERE-prefill-stall.md (this closes it)

ROOT CAUSE (two-part, both fixed)
---------------------------------
1) RING NEVER ARMED IN SERVED DAEMONS (the load-bearing bug).
   daemon.rs armed the SWA ring by translating SP_DAEMON_KVDECODE_RING_W ->
   std::env::set_var("SP_G4_KV_RING_W"). On Windows set_var = Win32
   SetEnvironmentVariableW, which the MSVC CRT env snapshot (what the CUDA
   lib's C getenv() reads) NEVER sees. gemma4_kv_open therefore read ring_W=0:
   every served daemon ran RING-OFF FULL-CACHE. At PMAX=20000 that allocates
   full-Pmax K/V for all 48 owner layers, oversubscribes the 12 GB 2060, and
   WDDM paging thrash makes per-token prefill superlinear (measured chunks
   6.9s -> 12.4s -> 22.6s per 128 tok; projected 20-50 min for n=1765) with
   GPU pinned at 99-100% — which any client timeout renders as "stalls
   forever, daemon alive". The historical B2 ring gates passed because their
   .bats set SP_G4_KV_RING_W in the SHELL (process-start env).
   FIX: daemon.rs crt_setenv() — mirror the var through _putenv_s (the CRT
   the statically-linked CUDA backend shares) so C getenv() sees it.
   Proof: served chat handle now logs "prefill START ... ringW=1024" and
   gemma4_kv_open prints "[g4-kv] RING mode: Wring=1024 Jmax=64".

2) NO INTERMEDIATE SYNC / SILENT LAUNCH ERRORS (robustness, fixed alongside).
   gemma4_kv_prefill queued n * ~700 async launches with zero drains and only
   checked errors at the terminal sync. FIX: chunked drain every
   SP_KV_PREFILL_SYNC tokens (default 128) + fail-fast with token index +
   SP_KV_PREFILL_LOG=1 progress/chunk-time telemetry (the instrument that
   found root cause #1). Pure control flow; computed bytes unchanged.

GATE (DONE-WHEN from the handoff)
