Daemon: run_console.bat (PMAX=20000, RING_W=1024, SP_PERSIST_KV=1, bx default)
  cmd: set SP_WORDS=1300 && python tests\perf\_g_bigprompt_probe.py
  ->  WORDS=1300  time=98.2s  out_chars=6  got_DONE=True          [GREEN]
  cmd: set SP_WORDS=200  && python tests\perf\_g_bigprompt_probe.py
  ->  WORDS=200   time=12.0s  out_chars=5  got_DONE=True          [GREEN]
Chunk telemetry (ring ON): 4.9s -> 8.5s per 128 tok, flattening past
dpos=1024 (SWA window capped by the ring) — exactly the O(1)-context shape.
Ring OFF (same build, control): 6.9/12.4/22.6s and rising at dpos<384.

HONEST SCOPE / OPEN EDGES
-------------------------
- 98.2s for a cold 1765-token prefill is CORRECT but not yet product-fast.
  Warm turns are O(suffix) via SP_PERSIST_KV. Follow-on levers (contract §T1):
  batched prefill default for cold big heads (SP_KV_PREFILL_BATCH=1 exists;
  float non-bx chat speed mode), and a packed-int8 batched GEMM (the batch
  path's gemm_w_lift dequant->f32-cublas is the cost center).
- The batched path at n=1764 under the RING-OFF config also thrashed (>12
  min, killed); re-measure under ring-ON before promoting any batch default.
- Client timeouts: probe uses 240s; gateway/console should surface prefill
  progress (SSE heartbeat) rather than sit silent — filed in §T4 (UI).

